#Pipe-fn binding: `name:|stage. | stage. | ...` desugars to a function
 that threads its arg through each stage. The `:` and first `|` must
 be adjacent — that's the marker that says "build a function from the
 following pipe". Subsequent `|`s follow normal pipeline spacing.#

inc:{n:_}(+!(n. 1))

#Single stage — equivalent to aliasing the function.#
flip:|inc.
assert!(flip!5 6)

#Two stages — point-free composition.#
twice:|inc.|inc.
assert!(twice!5 7)
assert!(twice!100 102)

#Spaces around later `|`s are fine; only the `:|` must be tight.#
twiceLoose:|inc. | inc.
assert!(twiceLoose!5 7)

#Mixing named functions and partials.#
flow:|inc.|*'2.|+'1.
assert!(flow!3 9)

#Pipe-fn is a first-class function value — usable wherever a fn goes.#
assert!(map!(twice. (1 2 3)) (3 4 5))
assert!(5?twice. 7)

#Text pipeline — normaliser.#
norm:|trim.|lower.
assert!(norm!HELLO hello)
